{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bcy2rj8az","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DnxaNFzXdz3Zu3wVB327Ye","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run1-repo/2aec8612-26e9-458d-b418-b812afb553c9/tasks/bcy2rj8az.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_2\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nPeople notice the single most lopsided stretch of a sequence — the contiguous run of flips in which heads most outnumber tails (or tails most outnumber heads), even when it is not one unbroken streak (HHTHH is a three-heads excess) — and that one striking local excess makes the sequence look less random by a shared weight. This sits on top of the current best judgement (each person's own ideal switching rate and sensitivity to it, personal weights on overall heads/tails imbalance and the longest streak, shared weights on the final streak, mirror symmetry and run-length variety, and a personal guessing rate); because a strictly alternating sequence never builds a local excess beyond one flip while a slightly less alternating one with a repeat or two clustered together does, it predicts that among two highly alternating sequences people choose the more alternating one more often than the best model does (the critique's high-alternation discrepancy).\nEOF\necho most_lopsided_stretch_aversion > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc=open('/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/models/run_length_variety_preference.py').read()\ndoc_end=src.index('import numpy')\ndoc='''\"\"\"Most lopsided stretch: one striking local heads/tails excess makes a sequence look designed.\n\nPeople notice the single contiguous stretch in which heads most outnumber tails\n(or vice versa) — the largest local excess, a maximum over sub-sequences, not\nonly unbroken streaks — and that one stretch makes the sequence look less random\nby a shared weight. This sits on the current best judgement (personal ideal\nswitching rate and sensitivity, personal weights on imbalance and the longest\nrun, shared weights on the final run, mirror symmetry and run-length variety,\npersonal lapse rate).\n\"\"\"\n\n'''\nsrc=doc+src[doc_end:]\nsrc=src.replace('''    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''','''    def lopsided_stretch(seq):\n        # Largest |#H - #T| over contiguous stretches = range of the running tally.\n        tally, lo, hi = 0, 0, 0\n        for x in seq:\n            tally += 1 if x == \"H\" else -1\n            lo = min(lo, tally)\n            hi = max(hi, tally)\n        return (hi - lo - 1) / (len(seq) - 1)\n\n    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''')\nsrc=src.replace('''        \"variety_b\": run_variety(b),\n''','''        \"variety_b\": run_variety(b),\n        \"lopsided_a\": lopsided_stretch(a),\n        \"lopsided_b\": lopsided_stretch(b),\n''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    participant_id = pm.Data(''','''    lopsided_a = pm.Data(\"lopsided_a\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    lopsided_b = pm.Data(\"lopsided_b\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    participant_id = pm.Data(''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    # Personal lapse''','''    # Shared penalty on the most lopsided stretch (positive: local excess looks designed).\n    eta = pm.Normal(\"eta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.5)\n\n    # Personal lapse''')\nsrc=src.replace('+ omega * variety_a','+ omega * variety_a - eta * lopsided_a').replace('+ omega * variety_b','+ omega * variety_b - eta * lopsided_b')\nassert src.count('eta * lopsided')==2\nopen('/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_2/candidate.py','w').write(src)\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"bbb18103-c242-4ca8-baf5-84747bfe5239","session_id":"2aec8612-26e9-458d-b418-b812afb553c9"}
